  "about": "Which real class each mock stands in for. MemberCheck (suite mock-honesty) fails on a mock class that is not listed here and on a mock member the real class does not offer to a script. real = the classes whose members the mock may offer (merged); jar = a file-name pattern when the real class is a mod's own and so is read from its jar with javap instead of from truth/engine-members.json; harness = members that are test plumbing, each with its reason (a member named t_* needs no entry); harness-class = a class no script under test is ever handed.",
